# Every text file is LF in the repository and in the working tree, on every
# platform. The repository was developed on Windows and a third of its files
# were CRLF; a scripted edit on Linux that rewrote one silently turned every
# line into a change, and a diff of seven thousand lines is one nobody can
# review. What is binary — the corpus documents, pictures, fonts — git tells
# apart on its own and leaves alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The corpus documents and their pictures are bytes, not text, and a reading
# is stamped with the document's digest: a line ending changed here would make
# every reading stale.
*.docx binary
*.docm binary
*.dotx binary
*.doc  binary
*.odt  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.xlsm binary
*.xltx binary
*.xls  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
